Operating the yamlover UI
description: the layout, navigation, views, the unified interaction model, and everyday editing
- >
  The `yamlover` server (`npx yamlover <root>`, or `npm start -- <root>` from the repo) serves a
  web app that browses a tree/DAG as a graph of nodes. This chapter covers how to drive that UI:
  the [layout](*::server:ui:layout), the [icons](*::server:ui:icons), the [representation tabs](*::server:ui:views), the unified
  [pan/zoom/select interaction model](*::server:ui:interaction) for materials,
  [annotating](*::server:ui:annotating), [editing a chapter](*::server:ui:editing), and
  [upload](*::server:ui:upload).
- >
  **Materials** are the leaf documents a node carries - prose (Markdown, AsciiDoc, marklower,
  chapters), images, KML/KMZ maps, PDFs, DjVu scans, spreadsheets, and so on. Each is shown by a
  renderer; the interaction rules are the same across them by design. (A chapter embeds media
  **structurally**: a body element - a pointer to a media member, or a chunk that is one media URL -
  [inlines](*::documents:marklower:embeds) an image, a video, or an audio track as its own figure.)
